==English==
===Etymology===
From the Italian ''[[arpeggiare]]'', to play a [[harp]].

===Noun===
'''arpeggio''' 
{{wikipedia}}
#{{music}} The notes of a chord played individually instead of simultaneously, usually moving from lowest to highest.
